== UI and Quality of Life Mods

Mods in this category improve the user interface and add convenience features without changing core gameplay. Every card below is verified against its Nexus Mods page (see STATUS.md for the decision register).

=== The StarUI Suite

The StarUI series (by *m8r98a4f2*) is the standard UI foundation for Starfield on PC. The original pages have not been updated since late 2024; install community compatibility patches (search "StarUI patch" / "thesamich") if a menu misbehaves after a game update.

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/773")[*StarUI Inventory*]

Overhauls every inventory screen for PC: compact rows, sortable columns (value, weight, damage), item tag icons, and a category sidebar.

- *Author:* m8r98a4f2
- *Version:* 2.4.1 (updated 2024-10-04)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *Impact:* UI only — no gameplay values change

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/3444")[*StarUI HUD*]

Reworks the in-world HUD: compact, configurable widgets for hit markers, XP, locations, and enemy health.

- *Author:* m8r98a4f2
- *Version:* 1.3 (updated 2024-10-01)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *Impact:* UI only

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/4966")[*StarUI Workbench*]

Redesigns the weapon, spacesuit, and industrial workbench screens with compact lists and quality-of-life filters.

- *Author:* m8r98a4f2
- *Version:* 1.2 (updated 2024-10-02)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *Impact:* UI only

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/5766")[*StarUI Outpost*]

